["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Snowshoe hare is the cheapest, longest and most forgiving hunt in Region 3, and the best classroom for your .22. It also carries one disease you must respect.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 366\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Grid of small animals and whether you may hunt them, 90 to 98 percent. Snowshoe hare: small game, Region 3 season 1 August to 30 April. Columbian ground squirrel: private land only, with permission. Eastern cottontail and grey squirrels: Schedule C, no licence needed, but they do not live near Heffley Creek. Nuttall&#x27;s cottontail: protected, Okanagan, no season. White tailed jackrabbit: protected, no season. Red squirrel: not for hunters, trapping only.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"366\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Small game: who you may hunt (90 to 98%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"36\" width=\"190\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(48 92) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snowshoe</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">hare</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Small game</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R3: Aug 1 to Apr 30</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"36\" width=\"190\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6ead2\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(244 96) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M-10 0 Q-34 -10 -26 -30 Q-14 -40 -12 -18Z\" fill=\"#b08a5a\"/><ellipse rx=\"14\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#b08a5a\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#b08a5a\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ground</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">squirrel</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Private land only</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">with permission</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"146\" width=\"190\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(48 202) scale(0.7)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cottontail,</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"193\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grey squirrel</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Schedule C</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Not near Heffley Ck</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"146\" width=\"190\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f3dcd6\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(244 202) scale(0.7)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#8a7a6a\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nuttall&#x27;s</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"193\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cottontail</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Protected</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Okanagan: no season</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"256\" width=\"190\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f3dcd6\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(48 312) scale(0.9)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#b8a888\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#b8a888\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#b8a888\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#b8a888\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#b8a888\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White tailed</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"303\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">jackrabbit</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"326\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Protected</text>\n  <text x=\"128\" y=\"343\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">no season</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"256\" width=\"190\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f3dcd6\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(244 316) scale(1.0)\"><path d=\"M-10 0 Q-34 -10 -26 -30 Q-14 -40 -12 -18Z\" fill=\"#a0522d\"/><ellipse rx=\"14\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#a0522d\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#a0522d\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"303\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">squirrel</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"326\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Not for hunters</text>\n  <text x=\"326\" y=\"343\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">trapping only</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Region 3 snowshoe hare: 1 August to 30 April, 10 a day <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Gloves on: tularemia is rare but real <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this session covers</summary><ul><li>In BC law, small game is fox, raccoon, coyote, skunk, snowshoe hare and game birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>No species licence; your basic resident hunting licence covers small game <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Region 3 snowshoe hare: Aug 1 to Apr 30, 10 a day <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Cottontails, European rabbits and grey squirrels are \"Schedule C\": no licence, no closed season, no bag limit, but they live far from Heffley Creek <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Red squirrels and ground squirrels are not game for a hunter: trapping only, or private land only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Tularemia, \"rabbit fever\", is rare in BC but real. Gloves, no sick animals, cook it through <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>List</th><th>What it means <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Small game</td><td>Seasons and limits</td><td>Snowshoe hare, fox, raccoon, coyote, skunk, game birds</td></tr><tr><td>Schedule B</td><td>Private land: protect property. Crown land: open seasons</td><td>Hare, ground squirrel, marmot, porcupine, skunk, raccoon, crows</td></tr><tr><td>Schedule C</td><td>No licence, no season, no limit</td><td>Cottontail, European rabbit, grey squirrel, bullfrog, starling</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>All other rules still apply: hours, no shooting areas, vehicles <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact definitions and full lists</summary><p>\"SMALL GAME - includes fox, raccoon, coyote, skunk, snowshoe hare and game birds.\" (Synopsis page 4) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></p><p>\"GAME BIRD - means any grouse, partridge, quail, pheasant, ptarmigan, migratory game bird, or wild turkey.\" (Synopsis page 3) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></p><ul><li><strong>Schedule B</strong> animals may be killed on private land to protect property, with no licence or season; on Crown land you follow the open seasons <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. The list includes snowshoe hare, Columbian ground squirrel, yellow bellied marmot, porcupine, striped skunk, raccoon, crows and magpies <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li><strong>Schedule C</strong> animals have no closed season or bag limit, no edible portion rule and no report; you do not need a hunting licence for them <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. The list: American bullfrog, green frog, snapping turtle, North American opossum, eastern cottontail, European rabbit, nutria, gray squirrels, fox squirrels, house sparrow, European starling and rock dove <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>All other hunting rules still apply to Schedule B and C: hours, no shooting areas, vehicle rules, no trafficking in meat <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. If you injure one you must kill it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Feral pigs need a hunting licence unless on your own land, and a Compulsory Report anywhere in BC <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Red, Douglas and northern flying squirrels are furbearing animals with trapping seasons, not hunting seasons <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snowshoe-hare-summer.jpg\" alt=\"Snowshoe hare in its brown coat, Banff. Grey brown body, dark ear tips, big dark eye.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snowshoe hare in its brown coat, Banff. Grey brown body, dark ear tips, big dark eye. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Martin Kraft, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MK04608_Snowshoe_Hare_(Banff).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A hare, not a rabbit: 1.2 to 1.6 kg, huge furred hind feet <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Brown in summer, white in winter <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snowshoe-hare-winter.jpg\" alt=\"Snowshoe hare in its white winter coat. Look at the huge furred hind feet: the snowshoes.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snowshoe hare in its white winter coat. Look at the huge furred hind feet: the snowshoes. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: D. Gordon E. Robertson, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowshoe_Hare,_Shirleys_Bay.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Snowshoe hare coat colour by month, 85 percent. White from about October to February. Moulting to brown in March and April. Brown from May to July. Moulting to white in August and September. On the wet southwest coast hares stay brown all year. Below, the Region 3 season runs from 1 August to 30 April, 10 a day, 98 percent, so it covers the white coat months.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snowshoe hare coat, by month (85%)</text>\n  <text x=\"29.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text>\n  <text x=\"60.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text>\n  <text x=\"91.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mar</text>\n  <text x=\"122.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n  <text x=\"153.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">May</text>\n  <text x=\"184.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n  <text x=\"215.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jul</text>\n  <text x=\"246.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n  <text x=\"277.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n  <text x=\"308.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n  <text x=\"339.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n  <text x=\"370.5\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n  <rect x=\"14\" y=\"66\" width=\"372\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4f4f4\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"138\" y=\"66\" width=\"93\" height=\"44\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/>\n  <rect x=\"76\" y=\"66\" width=\"62\" height=\"44\" fill=\"#c9bba6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"231\" y=\"66\" width=\"62\" height=\"44\" fill=\"#c9bba6\"/>\n  <text x=\"51.199999999999996\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White</text>\n  <text x=\"107\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moult</text>\n  <text x=\"184.5\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brown</text>\n  <text x=\"262\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Moult</text>\n  <text x=\"339.5\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(70 170) scale(1.4)\"><ellipse stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#f4f4f4\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#f4f4f4\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#f4f4f4\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#f4f4f4\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#f4f4f4\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Winter</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(200 170) scale(1.4)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Summer</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wet southwest</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">coast: brown</text>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">all year</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 3 season (98%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"14\" y=\"250\" width=\"124\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"231\" y=\"250\" width=\"155\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <text x=\"76\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">to Apr 30</text>\n  <text x=\"308.5\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">from Aug 1</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 a day</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: biology in full</summary><ul><li>A hare, not a rabbit: born furred with eyes open; adults 1.2 to 1.6 kg <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Grey brown in summer, white in winter, with huge furred hind feet; moults in August to September and March to April <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>On the wet southwest coast of BC, hares stay brown all year <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Home range about 6 to 10 ha, laced with packed trails called runways that show up after the first snow <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Numbers rise and crash on a cycle of about 10 years <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Food: leafy plants in summer; twigs, buds and bark of shrubs and conifers in winter, clipped up to 45 cm above the snow <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Predators: lynx, fox, coyote, mink, great horned owl, goshawk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Small tracks. Snowshoe hare: two big hind prints side by side land ahead of two small front prints, making a Y that points the way it went. Grouse: 3 toes forward and 1 short toe back, about 5 to 7 cm, in a single zig zag line.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hare and grouse</text>\n  <rect x=\"15\" y=\"45\" width=\"175\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"210\" y=\"45\" width=\"175\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eef2f6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"85\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"24\"/><ellipse cx=\"125\" cy=\"85\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"24\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"102\" cy=\"140\" r=\"8\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"170\" r=\"8\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M102 225 V200\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M102 60 l-8 14 h16 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">front</text>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">small</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">hind</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">big</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n    <g transform=\"translate(275 200)\"><path d=\"M0 0 V-22 M0 0 L-12 -18 M0 0 L12 -18 M0 0 V7\"/></g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(320 150)\"><path d=\"M0 0 V-22 M0 0 L-12 -18 M0 0 L12 -18 M0 0 V7\"/></g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(278 100)\"><path d=\"M0 0 V-22 M0 0 L-12 -18 M0 0 L12 -18 M0 0 V7\"/></g>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M355 120 l-8 14 h16 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M355 220 V134\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hare: a Y</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">big hind prints lead</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grouse: 3 + 1</text>\n  <text x=\"297\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5 to 7 cm, one line</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Young pine, willow, alder, 10 to 20 year cutblocks (Tip).</li><li>Dawn, dusk and grey days <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the Region 3 row and where to look</summary><ul><li>Region 3 row, page 34: \"SNOWSHOE HARE | 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44 | Aug 1 - Apr 30 | 10 (daily)\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></li><li>Young lodgepole pine, willow and alder thickets, cutblocks 10 to 20 years old, and swampy spruce edges (Tip).</li><li>Dawn and dusk, and overcast days; in deep winter they sit in \"forms\" (packed beds) under low branches and move on the runways at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The season covers deer season; carry a small game licence mindset and a .22 in October (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Animal</th><th>Region 3 rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Columbian ground squirrel</td><td>Private land only, with permission <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Raccoon</td><td>No closed season, no limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Gloves: roundworm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Skunk</td><td>Private land, property protection only <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Nuttall's cottontail, jackrabbit</td><td>Protected: never <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Red squirrel</td><td>Off limits to hunters <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every animal in full</summary><ul><li><strong>Columbian ground squirrel:</strong> Region 3 \"No Closed Season, NBL\", <strong>private land only</strong> with the landowner's permission <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Common on ranch pasture in spring and summer (Tip).</li><li><strong>Raccoon:</strong> Region 3 no closed season, no bag limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Raccoons carry a roundworm that can infect people; gloves and care with the gut <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><strong>Skunk:</strong> Schedule B; no Region 3 season row, so private land property protection only in Region 3 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><strong>Cottontails and rabbits:</strong> eastern cottontail and European rabbit are Schedule C and live in introduced pockets of southwest BC, not in Region 3 (60%, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> where). <strong>Nuttall's cottontail</strong> and <strong>white tailed jackrabbit</strong> in the Okanagan are protected: no season <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li><strong>Grey squirrels:</strong> Schedule C; introduced in the Lower Mainland and on south Vancouver Island <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Native red squirrels are off limits to hunters <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Look past the deer. Left, crossed: a deer stands on a skyline with a house beyond it, no shot. Right, ticked: a deer stands in front of a steep dirt hillside that stops the bullet, a safe backstop.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#efe2d6\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <path d=\"M8 200 L196 180 L196 240 L8 240 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><rect x=\"140\" y=\"140\" width=\"34\" height=\"26\"/><polygon points=\"134,140 157,120 180,140\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(80 178)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M30 172 L150 156\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 70 L130 130 M130 70 L60 130\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"6\" opacity=\".9\"/>\n  <path d=\"M204 240 L204 100 C 260 80, 330 60, 392 70 L392 240 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".55\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(300 200)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M330 90 l12 12 l26 -30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">House beyond: no</text>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dirt bank: yes</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Know what the bullet hits after the deer</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Head shot on a sitting hare, 25 to 50 m (27 to 55 yd) (Tip).</li><li>Dirt behind every shot. A .22 skips off ice and water (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: hours, loads, closures and snaring</summary><ul><li>Rimfire is legal for all small game and for grouse, ptarmigan and turkey among the birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Air guns and shotguns are legal too <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Head or neck shots at 25 to 50 m (27 to 55 yd) save all the meat (Tip). Wait for a sitting hare; a shotgun with 6 shot is better for running ones (Tip).</li><li>A .22 bullet skips off frozen ground and water and travels over a kilometre; find a dirt <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Backstop\">Backstop</button> every shot (Tip).</li><li>Subsonic 40 grain hollow points are quiet and plenty for hares (Tip).</li><li>No shooting within no shooting areas, from a vehicle, or across a road allowance <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Snaring hares is allowed in the open season with a hunting licence and the trapper education course; the snare must be unbraided wire no heavier than 20 gauge <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><p>\"A person may snare snowshoe hare during the open season if they have a hunting licence and completed the trapper education course. The snare must be non-braided and no heavier than 20 gauge.\" (Synopsis page 13) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></p></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view of a thicket. The pusher walks slowly into the thicket. A snowshoe hare jumps up and runs away along its runway, then circles back around its home range to the runway crossing where the stander waits. Tip: hares circle back home. Agree zones of fire first.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"150\" ry=\"80\"/></g>\n  <path id=\"sb-hare-circle-p\" d=\"M150 150 C 220 90, 330 110, 320 170 S 160 250, 110 200 S 90 130, 60 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Runway</text>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(1.0)\"><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-18\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pusher</text></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"360 260;220 160;220 160\" keyTimes=\"0;.5;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60 180) scale(1.0)\"><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stander</text>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.6)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" begin=\"3s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#sb-hare-circle-p\"/></animateMotion></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8s\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"250\" width=\"280\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">It circles back home (Tip)</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A pushed hare circles back to its runway. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A: still hunt the runways. B: push and stand. C: track in fresh snow (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Option A with the .22 on a snowy morning in December. Ten hares a day is a limit you will never need.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the three options, pros and cons</summary><h3>Option A: still hunt the runways</h3><ul><li>Walk slowly through young pine or willow, stop often, look for the black eye and ear tips of a sitting hare.</li><li>Pros: works alone, any snow (Tip).</li><li>Cons: hares freeze and you walk past them.</li></ul><h3>Option B: two hunters and a push</h3><ul><li>One walks the thicket, one stands on a runway crossing with a shotgun.</li><li>Pros: hares circle back to their home range (Tip).</li><li>Cons: zones of fire must be agreed before the first step.</li></ul><h3>Option C: tracking after fresh snow</h3><ul><li>Follow a fresh trail to the form, approach from downwind, shoot the sitting hare.</li><li>Pros: teaches tracking for every other animal (Tip).</li><li>Cons: slow.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four cards on cleaning hares safely because of tularemia, 85 to 95 percent. Wear gloves and a mask, every animal, every time. Never skin an animal found dead. A swollen, spotted liver or spleen goes in the bin, 60 percent. Cook the meat through until there is no pink at the bone.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Clean hares safely (85 to 95%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"36\" width=\"190\" height=\"124\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M80 54 h40 v34 q-20 10 -40 0z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gloves and mask</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Every animal,</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">every time (85%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"36\" width=\"190\" height=\"124\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(300 70) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(-15 14 -26)\"/><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"-26\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#9b8466\" transform=\"rotate(10 20 -26)\"/><circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"-10\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-14\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#9b8466\"/></g><path d=\"M316 50 l20 20 M336 50 l-20 20\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Found dead? Leave it</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Never skin an animal</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">found dead (95%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"166\" width=\"190\" height=\"124\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#7a2f2f\"/><g fill=\"#fff\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"196\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"104\" cy=\"204\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"194\" r=\"3\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spotted liver: bin it</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Swollen, spotted liver</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">or spleen (60%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"166\" width=\"190\" height=\"124\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"270\" y=\"186\" width=\"60\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M280 186 q4 -12 0 -20 M300 186 q4 -12 0 -20 M320 186 q4 -12 0 -20\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cook it through</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No pink at</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the bone (85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sick looking, slow hare? Do not touch it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Ulcer, fever, swollen nodes after cleaning: see a doctor (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: tularemia in full</summary><ul><li>Tularemia is caused by the bacterium Francisella tularensis; in BC it is reported occasionally, mostly in beavers, muskrats, voles, hares and rabbits <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>BC has about 0 to 2 human cases a year (search preview) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>People catch it by handling live or dead animals, by tick bites, by eating undercooked meat, or from contaminated water <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Human signs: a persistent ulcer where the skin was cut, fever, chills, feeling ill, swollen lymph nodes; antibiotics work when it is caught <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>The BC fact sheet rule: do not skin animals found dead <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Wear gloves and a mask while cleaning hares and rodents <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Wash hands and knives; cover cuts (Tip).</li><li>Thoroughly cook wild game before eating <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. A hare with a swollen, spotted liver or spleen goes in the bin, not the pot (hunter lore) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>A sick looking, slow hare is a hare you do not touch <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Check yourself for ticks after hunting brush in spring and fall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hare</th><th>How (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Young</td><td>Fry</td></tr><tr><td>Old</td><td>Soak in salt water overnight, stew 2 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Any</td><td>Cook until no pink at the bone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: cooking in full</summary><ul><li>Hare is lean, dark and strong; soak in salt water overnight, then braise or stew for 2 hours (Tip).</li><li>Young hares fry; old hares stew (Tip).</li><li>Cook until no pink remains at the bone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Take the meat home: wasting the edible parts of game is unlawful <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Do this instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A .22 at a hare on ice or a skyline</td><td>Dirt backstop, or no shot</td></tr><tr><td>Skinning bare handed</td><td>Gloves, every time</td></tr><tr><td>A \"rabbit\" in the south Okanagan</td><td>Could be a protected Nuttall's cottontail</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the mistakes in full</summary><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Shooting a .22 at a hare on a skyline or on ice with no backstop.</li><li>Skinning bare handed and nicking a finger.</li><li>Shooting a \"rabbit\" in the south Okanagan that was a protected Nuttall's cottontail.</li></ul></aside></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snowshoe-hare-winter.jpg\" alt=\"A deer with the volume turned down.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A deer with the volume turned down. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: D. Gordon E. Robertson, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowshoe_Hare,_Shirleys_Bay.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>A hare is a deer with the volume turned down. Hunt it the same way: slow, into the wind, eyes before feet.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: one more rule, and this week's field task</summary><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Gloves on, every animal, every time.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>This week: walk a young pine cutblock after fresh snow, count the runways you cross in 200 m, and find one form.</p></aside></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"s4-small-game-start\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s4-small-game-start:0\"><span>Confirm my MU is in 3-12 to 3-20 or 3-26 to 3-44</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s4-small-game-start:1\"><span>Buy nitrile gloves and a mask for the cleaning kit</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s4-small-game-start:2\"><span>Zero the .22 at 40 m with the ammunition I hunt with</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s4-small-game-start:3\"><span>Find a cutblock with hare runways near Heffley Creek</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s4-small-game-start:4\"><span>Learn the tularemia signs: ulcer, fever, swollen nodes</span></label></div>","<ul><li>BC synopsis, BC Wildlife Health, Canadian Wildlife Health Cooperative, BC Centre for Disease Control, Hinterland Who's Who. Checked 2026-10-01.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source, page and date checked</summary><ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">full PDF</a>, read directly: definitions pages 3 and 4; fees page 8; Schedule B and C page 11; hours and unlawful acts page 12; weapons and snaring page 13; Region 3 page 34; Region 8 page 67; trapping seasons page 76; checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></li><li>BC Wildlife Health, <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/environment/plants-animals-and-ecosystems/wildlife-wildlife-habitat/wildlife-health/wildlife-health-documents/tularemia.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tularemia in British Columbia fact sheet</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>Canadian Wildlife Health Cooperative, <a href=\"https://www.cwhc-rcsf.ca/docs/fact_sheets/Tularemia_Fact_Sheet.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tularemia fact sheet</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li>BC Centre for Disease Control, <a href=\"https://www.bccdc.ca/health-info/diseases-conditions/tick-borne-diseases/tularemia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tularemia</a>, search preview only, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>Hinterland Who's Who, <a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/mammals/snowshoe-hare.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Snowshoe hare</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li>Wikipedia, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_gray_squirrel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Eastern gray squirrel</a>, BC introductions, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul></details>"]